<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samia Suluhu Hassan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1960</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samia Suluhu Hassan is a Tanzanian politician from Zanzibar who became the country's first woman president in March 2021. A member of the ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chama-cha-mapinduzi">Chama Cha Mapinduzi</a>, she had served as vice-president from 2015 and succeeded on the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-magufuli">John Magufuli</a>. Her government at first eased restrictions on the press and opposition and reversed her predecessor's approach to the Covid-19 pandemic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samia-suluhu-hassan.jpg" alt="Samia Suluhu Hassan" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kremlin.ru · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samia_Suluhu_at_the_XXIX_St_Petersburg_International_Economic_Forum_-_2026_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
